<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/inventions?focus=water-wheel">Inventions &amp; Discoveries</a> · Energy and power</p><h1 class="enc-title">Water wheel</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">4th century BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/4th-century-bce">4th century BCE</a> · Also known as waterwheel</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">A water wheel is a machine that turns the energy of flowing or falling water into power through a large wheel with blades or buckets on its rim; it first appeared in ancient <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> in the 4th century BCE, where wheels lifted water for irrigation. By the 3rd century BCE they turned millstones in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/near-east">Near East</a>, and in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> from 31 CE they drove blast-furnace bellows for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cast-iron">cast iron</a>. They supplied power for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/industrial-revolution">Industrial Revolution</a> until the turbine of Benoît Fourneyron, whose first model dates from 1827, began to displace them.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/water-wheel.jpg" alt="Water wheel" width="320" height="180" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Spike · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Brucker_Wasserrad_01.webm" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="inv-entry"><h2 class="enc-section-title">On the inventions tree</h2><dl class="inv-entry-facts"><div><dt>First known</dt><dd>4th century BCE</dd></div><div><dt>Where</dt><dd>Egypt</dd></div></dl><p class="inv-entry-note"><span class="inv-k">Note</span>The first watermills have been placed in Persia before 350 BCE and in Byzantium and Alexandria in the 3rd century BCE.</p><div class="inv-entry-rel"><span class="inv-k">Built on</span><a class="inv-chip" href="/encyclopedia/irrigation">Irrigation<span>c. 6000 BCE</span></a><a class="inv-chip" href="/encyclopedia/wheel">Wheel<span>before 4000 BCE</span></a></div><div class="inv-entry-rel"><span class="inv-k">Led to</span><a class="inv-chip" href="/encyclopedia/windmill">Windmill<span>9th century</span></a></div><p class="enc-article-foot"><a class="enc-random-link" href="/inventions?focus=water-wheel">See it on the inventions tree &rarr;</a></p></section>
